1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,311
Bengal muslin was among the finest cloths ever woven. The cotton, and the skill, are gone.

2
00:00:08,611 --> 00:00:18,502
In 2013, India's last known speaker of Majhi was eighty years old. His language had fifteen words for river.

3
00:00:18,802 --> 00:00:27,533
Japan's registered craft workforce fell from about 288,000 to under 50,000.

4
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:34,644
And in every company, the reason behind a decision often lives in one person's head.

5
00:00:34,944 --> 00:00:41,215
When an expert leaves, the why leaves with them. Agamya keeps it.

6
00:00:41,415 --> 00:00:42,215
So this is my mother.

7
00:00:42,215 --> 00:00:50,415
Today she is going to show us one of the most famous recipes from our native place, Satara.

8
00:00:50,415 --> 00:00:53,215
Bharati (Marathi): Hello. Now we'll make a famous recipe from Satara.

9
00:00:54,015 --> 00:00:56,015
Bharati: For that, we need peanuts.

10
00:00:56,415 --> 00:00:58,115
Moti (Marathi): The peanuts are roasted, right?

11
00:00:58,115 --> 00:00:59,415
Bharati: Yes, roast the peanuts.

12
00:00:59,415 --> 00:01:01,415
Moti: How do you make sure the peanuts don't burn while roasting?

13
00:01:01,415 --> 00:01:03,915
Bharati: Roast them on a low flame.

14
00:01:04,415 --> 00:01:06,415
Moti: On a low flame they roast properly, right?

15
00:01:06,415 --> 00:01:07,415
Bharati: Yes, they roast well.

16
00:01:07,415 --> 00:01:09,215
Moti: How much should the onion be roasted?

17
00:01:09,415 --> 00:01:11,915
Bharati: Until it turns reddish.

18
00:01:12,415 --> 00:01:13,415
Moti: Until reddish, okay.

19
00:01:13,415 --> 00:01:14,415
Bharati: Yes, then add red chilli powder.

20
00:01:14,415 --> 00:01:16,715
You can see it is generated. You can play it.

21
00:01:16,815 --> 00:01:24,615
Lesson (Marathi): First roast the peanuts. Roast them on a low flame so they don't burn.

22
00:01:24,615 --> 00:01:29,015
From Kiran's account: Bharati's Kitchen shared the recipe with her.

23
00:01:29,415 --> 00:01:34,315
She has access to all of this.

24
00:01:34,315 --> 00:01:39,215
She can listen in Hindi, Marathi, Kannada: the language she prefers.

25
00:01:39,215 --> 00:01:41,715
If everything is okay, export it for agents.

26
